AC8 first run (superseded recipe, kept per environmental-FAIL discipline):

Recipe: fake session + ALL GET /api/* passed through to real dev backend (5788), writes intercepted.
Result: three pages #root non-empty, pageerror 0, unhandledrejection 0, zero business writes,
/api/task/all 200, /api/home 200 — BUT console showed 401 resource-load errors
(4 on /, 10 on /task, 4 on /task/new) and the /task/new page degraded to the logged-out
「登录已过期，请重新登录 / 请先登录」 state (innerText 188 chars).

Attribution: the fake session's token is NOT a real credential ⇒ authed GETs legitimately
return 401 ⇒ the app's auth-expiry interceptor (auth-expiry-20261017 work) clears the fake
session ⇒ page renders the logged-out state. That is correct app behavior against a bogus
token — environment noise of the probe, not a defect of this batch.

Resolution: re-ran with the established recipe (implementer probe-job-form.mjs / item-QA
probe-form.mjs): ONLY /api/currencies passes to the real backend; all other /api/* GETs are
stubbed 200 {success:true,data:[]} so no 401 noise is manufactured. See ac8-pages.json (rerun).
The real-backend 200s for /api/task/all + /api/home are covered by the direct curl readings
(ac8_api_task_all.body.json / ac8_api_home.body.json + ac8-api-status.txt).
